The pinned Augists Sylvan fork supplies worker reference infrastructure.

The task decomposition, sharded canonicalization and temporary ownership design
are informed by MTPNDD, Copyright Augists and XJTU ANTS Netverify Lab,
also licensed under Apache License 2.0. PNDD storage and Boolean kernels are
new implementations, not a copy of MTPNDD's numerical leaves or caches.

The build-local Sylvan adapter changes only Boolean/ZDD node construction to
return an invalid sentinel on table exhaustion, and records node allocations.
It uses checked PNDD apply kernels, not upstream apply routines that assume
node creation cannot fail. The original dependency checkout is not modified.
Upstream copyright notices are retained in the fetched build sources.

The build-local Lace adapter adds bounded sleeping to barrier and TOGETHER
completion waits when workers outnumber the available processing units. It
preserves the pinned dependency checkout and its upstream copyright notices.
The affinity feature check enables GNU declarations so Linux CPU masks are
respected when deciding whether the worker pool is oversubscribed.

The MT extension draws backend/universe dispatch, dense import and fused
multiply-sum abstraction designs from the Java MTNDD branch of XJTU-NetVerify/NDD
at 8d343b3 (Apache-2.0). It adds numeric terminals and checked arithmetic to the
shared compact parallel manager rather than copying the Java global edge stack.
See mtndd/docs/MIGRATION.md for provenance and numerical policy differences.
